# Mini keypads / macropads identifying as USB vendor 0x1189.
# (Commonly called "CH57x" by convention; the actual MCU varies.)
# Product ids used across the family, under vendor 0x1189 and 0x514c:
#   8830 8831 8832 8833 8840 8842 8850 8851 8890
#
# Keep this list in step with MODELS in index.html — a keypad missing here
# works on Windows and silently fails on Linux, because Chrome cannot open a
# hidraw node it has no permission for. A test in test-protocol.mjs enforces it.
#
# Grants the user of the active local seat read/write on the keypad's HID
# nodes, so a configurator (ch57x-keyboard-tool, probe.py, or a WebHID page
# in Chrome) can talk to it without root.
#
# MUST be numbered below 70. systemd's 70-uaccess.rules is what acts on the
# uaccess tag; a rule that adds the tag later than that is silently ignored.
KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1189|514c", \
  ATTRS{idProduct}=="8830|8831|8832|8833|8840|8842|8850|8851|8890", TAG+="uaccess"
